# 0004 NVRMAGDC: answer the K5 link-config command from the live panel timing
#
# Base:  NvGfx xe 5a19a73f36249efb99c44c3f9cb34603ef0c0eb8 (XeGfx 0.0.44)
# Files: kexts/NVRMAGDC/nvrm-agdc.cpp (modified)
#        kexts/NVRMAGDC/xe/Info.plist (modified: measured EDID, IOPCIFamily/IOGraphicsFamily libs)
#        kexts/NVRMAGDC/xe/firmware-timing.h (new)
#        kexts/NVRMAGDC/xe/panel-timing.h (new)
# Apply: patch -p1 < patches/0004-agdc-k5-panel-timing.patch
#
# IOPresentment only starts display-pipe transactions after AGDC answers the K5 link-config
# command (0x921) with the panel's timing.  The kext now probes the display engine on BAR0
# read-only (same 14 registers and frame counter as XeGfxIntelFB), validates a cached panel
# EDID against those live registers and the measured frame counter, and answers K5 from the
# result.  debug.xegfx_panel_probe captures one read-only Pipe A snapshot, and
# debug.xegfx_panel_timing_source / debug.xegfx_panel_probe_result report what was accepted.
# Without an exact match the kext declines the Intel display trial instead of guessing.
#

